Acknowledgements
================

Shuo is an application that calls locally-downloaded speech models. Model
weights are the property of their respective authors and are NOT redistributed
by this repository (they are fetched from ModelScope / Hugging Face at
install time by the user).

Primary ASR model (fine-tuned package, prompt-controlled output style):

- Base model: Qwen3-ASR-1.7B by Qwen Team — Apache License 2.0
  https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B
  Official repo: https://github.com/QwenLM/Qwen3-ASR
  Technical report: https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.21337
- GGUF conversion tooling: ggml-org/llama.cpp — MIT License
  Official GGUF release: https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/Qwen3-ASR-1.7B-GGUF
- The fine-tuned package (data, LoRA training, GGUF conversion/quantisation)
  was produced by OrientCOMPASS — https://github.com/OrientCOMPASS — as
  PR #1 of this repository. This project only hosts/distributes it
  (ModelScope: a2heng/shuo-asr-1.7b-gguf) and is NOT the model author.
- It is a LoRA fine-tune of the base model (transcription with
  prompt-controlled output style, in one pass); provenance (base / adapter /
  prompts / timestamp) is recorded in the package's shuo-model.json marker file.

Denoiser (bundled with the app):

- src-tauri/resources/denoise.onnx — streaming NFT_960 denoiser (48 kHz).

Runtime libraries: llama.cpp (MIT), ONNX Runtime (MIT, denoise only),
Tauri (MIT/Apache-2.0), cpal (Apache-2.0/MIT), ureq (MIT/Apache-2.0).
